         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_21>cific Ocean","container-title":"Earth and Planetary Science Letters","page":"345-361","volume":"232","issue":"3-4","source":"CrossRef","DOI":"10.1016/j.epsl.2004.12.009","ISSN":"0012821X","author":[{"family":"Ling","given":"Hong-Fei"},{"family":"Jiang","g</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_21>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_22>iven":"Shao-Yong"},{"family":"Frank","given":"Martin"},{"family":"Zhou","given":"Huai-Yang"},{"family":"Zhou","given":"Feng"},{"family":"Lu","given":"Zun-Li"},{"family":"Chen","given":"Xiao-Ming"},{"family":"Jiang","given":"Yao-Hui"},{"family":"Ge","given</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_22>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_23>":"Cheng-Dong"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2005",4]]},"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2014",1,21]],"season":"15:18:30"}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_23>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_3>3957-3974","volume":"61","issue":"18","source":"ScienceDirect","abstract":"Oceanic and atmospheric circulation patterns varied considerably during the Tertiary and Quaternary and influenced the geochemical cycles of elements in seawater. We report the fir</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_3>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_4>st resolution lead and neodymium isotopic record of such changes at a high time resolution in two depths profiles from a hydrogenous Feî—¸Mn crust. The crust, Va13-2, is located in the central Pacific (146Â°W, 9Â°25â€²N, 4830 m) and has previously been dated by</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_4>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_5> 230Th and 10Be. The first profile was drilled with a sample time resolution of âˆ¼3 kyr and allows evaluation of short-term changes to lead and neodymium sources to central Pacific seawater over the last 400 kyr (marine Î´18O stages 2 to 11). Longer-term ch</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_5>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_6>anges were monitored at lower time resolution in a second profile to an age of 10 Ma.\n\nShort-term variations in lead and neodymium isotope ratios are resolved in the high resolution profile (0 to 400 kyr). Superimposed on the short-term variations is a </pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_6>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_7>secular decrease in 206Pb204Pb ratios beginning at âˆ¼130 kyr in marine Î´18O stage 5, implying a change in the lead sources to the central Pacific. Lead and neodymium isotopic compositions indicate an increased influence from Central American eolian sources</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_7>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_8> to Pacific seawater at this time. Lead isotopes are found to be statistically more variable during interglacial than glacial periods. These observations are supported by the greater eolian dust fluxes found in sediment cores from the equatorial Pacific d</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_8>
         <pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_9>uring interglacial stages.\n\nThe most important paleoceanographic event of the last 10 Ma to affect Pacific seawater was the closure of the Panama gateway. Changes in lead and neodymium isotopes in Val3-2 during the last 10 Ma occurred along with gradual</pdfx:ZOTERO_BREF_VaOfawBEwayl_9>
